// Commercial cleaning page, built from content-plans/commercial-cleaning.md.
//
// THIS PAGE IS A HUB, NOT A LEAF. /commercial-cleaning/ is a top-level
// header item with FIFTEEN child pages under it (navigation.ts:143-172).
// The brief was written as a standalone service page and linked to none of
// them. The "What we clean" TagCloud below is not in the brief — it was
// added because a hub that doesn't link its cluster isn't a hub. See the
// plan's blocker 2.
//
// The audience is B2B: an office manager, practice manager, strata
// committee or venue owner choosing a cleaner for premises they are
// responsible for. Not a householder, and emphatically not an NDIS
// participant — see the §3 note.
//
// ── ✅ REWRITTEN AGAINST THE SEO COPY-REWRITE BRIEF, 17 September 2026 ────
//
// Brief: workbook row 25, "Commercial cleaning (hub)". Mapped primary
// `commercial cleaning` 3,600/mo, seven mapped secondaries, 5,940/mo across
// the cluster — minus `commercial cleaning services australia` (150/mo),
// which the brief excludes as national intent on the grounds that a regional
// operator ranking for a national term attracts enquiries it cannot service.
// No copy targets it and it is out of the addressable denominator.
//
// ⚠️ EVERY VOLUME IN THIS FILE COMES FROM THE KEYWORD MAPPING & METADATA
// WORKBOOK, WHICH CARRIES NO PULL DATE. DataForSEO, Ahrefs and Search Console
// were all unreachable when the brief was written, so no position,
// impression, click, CTR, difficulty or SERP-feature figure appears anywhere
// in it or here. The brief's own "is there a stronger primary keyword"
// check could not be run and is unanswered rather than settled.
//
// WHAT CHANGED: title and meta (§0), H1 and hero lead (§1), one primary CTA
// repeated in three places, an H2 over the definition block (§2), two pathway
// card bodies and a card label (§3), the Award argument split and de-fanged
// (§5), a note line under the premises pills (§7), the comparison table
// rebuilt for a workplace (§10), the testimonial carousel hidden (§9), the
// full 56-town footprint restored (§14), four of five branded FAQs (§11) and
// both FAQ headings (§11, §12).
//
// The primary keyword now appears contiguously in the title, the meta, the
// URL, the H1, the first sentence of the lead and two H2s. Three headings
// carry the service term, against one before.
//
// NOT DONE, and recorded in the brief rather than forgotten: the trust bar
// and the pathway-card routing module are both excluded from rewrite by
// standing rule, and `commercial floor cleaning services` (90/mo) gets no
// passage here because two child pages are better homes for it.
//
// BLOCKS LAUNCH:
//   - Screening, and it is still the first item. BFD §2.4 lists [insured] and
//     [police-checked] as unconfirmed. Card 3 no longer asserts either — it
//     carries a process promise instead, per §2.4's own rule — and the
//     approved meta description was NOT shipped because it publishes
//     "police-checked" as fact in a search result (see §0). Meanwhile the last
//     non-branded FAQ still tells readers that childcare work needs a Working
//     With Children Check and to "ask any cleaner to confirm which of their
//     team hold a current check". Those are DIFFERENT checks, the mega-menu
//     actively invites school and childcare enquiries, and the page still
//     asks a question about itself it cannot answer. One confirmation closes
//     the card, the meta and four sibling pages at once.
//   - QLD is unaddressed. The non-branded FAQ says "In NSW" (correct), but
//     footerContact says "Northern Rivers, NSW & Southern Gold Coast, QLD",
//     §14 now lists nine Queensland towns and `areaServed` was widened to
//     match. QLD's equivalent is a Blue Card, not a WWCC. Either confirm
//     commercial work crosses the border or revert §14, `areaServed` and the
//     subheading together — and the FAQ needs its QLD clause either way.
//   - The scope of work is missing entirely. See the §8 comment — the page
//     tells the reader to demand a task list four times and never shows one.
//   - How TLB invoices commercial clients. The bracket is out of card 2, but
//     only because a bracket addressed to TLB cannot sit in customer-facing
//     copy. The question is unanswered, not resolved.
//   - Three commercial testimonials with written permission to name the
//     business (BFD §12.1, §5.3). The carousel is hidden until they exist.
//   - The four trust-bar claims BFD §2.4 marks "Confirm": the retention
//     figure, the agency preferred-supplier wording, the client count and the
//     spread-teams claim. All four are live and none is verified.
//   - Sign-off on the two competitor columns in the comparison table,
//     including the new keys-and-alarms row. BFD §9.4 permits the table only
//     where the rows stay neutral and factual, and no cell in either column
//     has been checked.
//
// WORKBOOK CHANGE REQUESTS, raised against row 25:
//   - 🔴 The approved meta publishes "police-checked". Blocking; the brief's
//     replacement ships in its place. See §0.
//   - The approved title and meta both promise "on contract" while the page
//     sells no lock-in, no minimum term and no exit fee. The approved title
//     ships as approved; the meta does not, for the credential reason above.
//     See §0 for the suggested replacements.
//
// STILL NEEDS A DEVELOPER, none of it a copy problem:
//   - The whole site is `noindex, nofollow` via site-env.ts. Correct for
//     staging, fatal at launch — and the production URL currently 404s.
//   - The `LocalBusiness` JSON-LD below has empty telephone, email, logo,
//     image and all five address fields.
//   - No `FAQPage` schema on either FAQ section, no `Service` schema, no
//     `BreadcrumbList`. Two well-formed FAQ sections are already on the page.
//   - The site header carries two CTAs on every page, and "Get an instant
//     quote" should not appear on a commercial page at all: BFD §13.2 names
//     commercial as a service where condition drives the price, and §15 of
//     this page says the same thing in its own words. Template-level, so not
//     changed here.
//
// NOT BUILT, deliberately: credibility signals, hero video, "the why" — all
// empty in the brief. Precedent is deep-cleaning.astro, whose credibility
// block was filled on a reasonable assumption and removed again at TLB's
// direction.
