  'So the gap between two quotes is almost never a gap in margin. It is a gap in hours, or in how many tasks are on the list. Work out which before you compare the numbers, because a lower price for fewer hours is a different product, not a better deal.',
  'The number that matters is not the hourly rate. It is what is in the scope. Ask any cleaner exactly which tasks are included, how often they happen, and whether consumables like soap and paper are covered. We put ours in writing before we start, and we tell you straight when a clean has to happen after hours, because early starts, late finishes, weekends and public holidays all carry a penalty rate under the Award. No surprises, either way.',
